Given:

Ramu can build a wall alone in = 15 days

Ravan can build it alone = 10 days

Formula used:

Work = Efficiency × Time

Calculation:

Let the can complete the remaining work in X days.

One day work of Ramu = {1over15}

One day work of Ravan = {1over10}

5 days' work of Ramu = {5over15}={1over3}

Ramu and Ravan worked for 3 days together. 

3 days' work of Ramu and Ravan together = {3over15}+{3over10}={1over5}+{3over10}={10+15over50}={25over50}={1over2}

The remaining work = {1-{({1over3}+{1over2}})}={1-({2+3over 6})}=1-{5over6}={6-5over6}={1over6}

The remaining work completed by Ramu = {{1over6}over{1over15}}={15over6}=2.5 days

∴ The required result will be 2.5 days.
